---
globs: templates/**/*.html
---
## Templates Conventions

- **Layout**:
  - Define a main layout in `templates/layouts/base.html` using Go template blocks:
    {{define "base"}}
    <html>
      <head>{{block "head" .}}{{end}}</head>
      <body>
        {{template "components/nav" .}}
        <main>{{block "content" .}}{{end}}</main>
        {{block "scripts" .}}{{end}}
      </body>
    </html>
    {{end}}
- **Components**:
  - Place reusable parts in `templates/components/*.html`.
  - Each file should `{{define "components/name"}} ... {{end}}` and be included via `{{template "components/name" .}}`.
- **Pages**:
  - Place page templates in `templates/pages/*.html`.
  - Each page must define at least `{{define "content"}} ... {{end}}` to render within the base layout.
- **Lazy fragments**:
  - Place in `templates/lazy/*.html` and render via `Renderer.RenderLazyHTML` or `Renderer.LazyHandler`.
  - Files may define `{{define "fileName.html"}} ... {{end}}` and are executed by their base filename.
- **HTMX-aware rendering**:
  - Full render executes layout `base`.
  - Partial render (HTMX request and not boosted) executes only the `content` block.
  - Map-like data (e.g., `H`, `Fields`, `map[string]any`) is auto-augmented with `.HX` from request headers.
- **Helper funcs** (available in templates):
  - `concat(args...) string`: concatenates values.
  - `attr(map) HTML`: prints HTML attributes from `map[string]string` or `map[string]any`.
  - `partial(name, data) HTML`: renders a named partial from the shared set.